    "state": "MERIDIAN RENTALS — COURSE SERVICES AGREEMENT, EXECUTED 12 AUGUST\n\nParties and purpose. Meridian Rentals (the Provider) will administer room bookings, equipment access, and student registration support for the Northbridge Evening School’s autumn courses. The School’s contract administrator is Oren Nakamura. The agreement concerns administrative services only; it does not authorize either party to decide academic grades or waive tuition debts. The initial service period runs from 1 September through 20 December. The parties will use the shared service ledger as the record of completed support shifts and approved reimbursements.\n\nSection 4, staffing and invoices. Provider staff may submit reimbursement claims for approved travel and materials. Each claim must identify the staff member, the service date, the relevant course, and the amount. The School pays approved claims within 21 calendar days of receiving a complete claim. A claim lacking a receipt is incomplete unless the School’s administrator records a written exception. The Provider must not combine amounts for different staff members in a way that prevents review. The School may dispute a line item without withholding payment for undisputed items.\n\nOriginal Schedule B. The weekly evening-desk allowance is $180 per scheduled shift, payable only for shifts recorded as completed. If two staff members share one shift, the allowance is divided between them in the ledger; each person’s share is not a separate $180 allowance. Reimbursement for approved transit is separate from the desk allowance. The Provider must submit a monthly statement with its supporting ledger and receipts.\n\nAmendment 1, signed 28 August. For the October examination period only, the desk allowance is increased to $200 per completed shift. This change does not alter the allowance for September or November and does not change the rule for dividing an allowance when a shift is shared. All other terms of Schedule B remain in ef