    "state": "Policy page: Northbridge Pixel Guild — event notices\n\nWe are delighted when members take part in community events, and we try to make event notices as clear as possible. An event host may publish a notice in the guild calendar. The calendar entry is the official place to check the event time, game mode, and whether registration is required. A draft notice or a moderator’s private note does not by itself change the published entry.\n\nFor the Frostglass Cup, the published calendar entry currently reads: “Friendly practice lobby, no registration required, Saturday at 18:00 guild time.” Members may simply join the lobby. If the host later changes the event to a registered tournament, the calendar entry must be updated before members are expected to register.\n\nA moderator’s preliminary review note, added while checking the calendar, says: “Registration required; warn anyone who joins without signing up.” The note is not the event notice. The moderator then checked the actual published entry and confirmed that it still says friendly practice lobby and no registration required. No update has been made, and no separate host announcement changes that instruction. The preliminary note was copied into the review history for clarity, but the moderator marked it as an outdated assumption and asked members to follow the calendar entry.\n\nOur general event guidance asks everyone to use respectful language, avoid spamming the lobby, and give teammates room to participate. These courtesy rules apply to both practice sessions and tournaments. They do not turn a friendly practice lobby into a registered event. Members who are unsure are welcome to ask the host, but simply asking whether registration is needed does not count as registration and does not mean registration is required.\n\nThe guild is pleased to welcome new and returning players. Please check the published calendar before traveling to an event, and accept our apologies if an old draft or copied note c