ields, and the form has a green submission confirmation. Callum said he had mistaken the fact that no letters were attached for missing references. He changed his own comment aloud but did not edit the tracker during the meeting. The older note remains visible, so whoever reads the export should rely on the fields rather than assume the note was corrected.\n\nThe team also checked schedule availability. Uma had written, “Possible weekend conflict?” because the résumé describes a previous Monday-to-Friday job. That was a question, not evidence of unavailability. Esi checked the schedule box, and her application contains no request to avoid Saturdays. The group agreed the direct application answer is the relevant evidence. Nobody found a conflicting message from Esi.\n\nOn the minimum-experience question, the tracker has another comment from Callum: “Below minimum; only one year in relevant work.” The résumé’s dates and description do not support that summary. It shows work from February 2021 through February 2024 coordinating patient appointments and handling schedule adjustments. The role’s minimum is two years. Esi’s earlier unrelated retail position is also listed, but it is not needed to reach the threshold. The team said the comment may have come from an older draft of the résumé, although the source of the mistake is unknown.\n\nThe interview panel has not yet been assigned. No one recorded a pass or fail, and the hiring manager has not approved a shortlist. Esi has not withdrawn, and the application portal shows the file as submitted rather than draft. One meeting participant said, “It’s all settled, we can just tick complete,” but the group clarified that complete paperwork and a positive hiring decision are separate things. They agreed to keep the application in the ordinary review queue. The final discussion ended with a reminder to verify facts in the actual form and résumé before carrying a tracker comment forward.",
