    "state": "Forwarded note from Aiden Alvarez: “Can someone untangle this before the afternoon run? The job card says the customer caused the delay, and I have no idea whether that is actually what happened.”\n\nForwarded email thread, subject: Re: housing covers, revised slot\n\nFrom: Bao Moreau, dispatch\nTo: Larkspur Freight coordinator\n\nI am forwarding the chain because the job board currently says “customer postponed pickup,” and that is being used to explain why the finished covers sat on our rack. The cover plates for Saltmarsh Rentals were complete on Tuesday the 9th. Their agreed collection slot was Thursday the 11th, between 10 and noon. Our shop had the pallet wrapped and the paperwork ready by 9:30 that morning. The labels showed the customer’s receiving bay, not our loading bay, which was correct according to their latest delivery sheet.\n\nFrom: Saltmarsh Rentals receiving desk\nTo: Bao Moreau\n\nWe have not moved the pickup. Our driver is still scheduled for Thursday morning. The revised address sheet we sent last week only changes the unloading entrance; it does not change the date. Please confirm that your gate is open before ten, because the last driver waited outside while someone looked for the key.\n\nFrom: Bao Moreau\nTo: Saltmarsh Rentals receiving desk\n\nConfirmed, gate will be open. Sorry about the previous wait. We will have the pallet at the door.\n\nFrom: workshop administrator\nTo: production list\n\nI have put “customer postponed pickup” in the job notes. The receiving desk changed the sheet, and the sheet came through after the first schedule, so I assumed the date had shifted. I will leave the note unless someone has a better account.\n\nFrom: Saltmarsh Rentals receiving desk\nTo: Bao Moreau, copied to shop\n\nThe driver reached your gate at 10:42 on Thursday. He called twice and waited until 11:25. He says the gate was locked and the pallet was not outside. We have not rescheduled; please tell us when it is actually ready for collection. We need it for the maintenance crew on Monday.\n\nFrom: Bao Moreau\nTo: Saltmarsh Rentals receiving desk\n\nThat is on us. The gate key was with the person doing the machine check, and the pallet had been moved inside to make room for a delivery of sheet stock. We did not notice the truck had arrived until the driver called the second time. We can load it today, Friday, after 1 p.m. if that works.\n\nFrom: Saltmarsh Rentals receiving desk\nTo: Bao Moreau\n\nFriday at 1 p.m. works. To be clear, this is a new pickup slot because your gate was unavailable yesterday, not because we asked to postpone the original one.\n\nThe job-card note was not corrected. In the afternoon, the scheduler wrote: “Customer changed pickup day; no shop delay.” That summary is a verdict entered by our own staff, not a statement from the customer. It seems to have been inferred from the revised address sheet and the eventual Friday collection. The actual customer messages say that the date remained Thursday and that Friday was agreed only after the shop failed to release the pallet on Thursday.\n\nA second message from the customer arrived on Friday at 12:38: “Our van is on the way for the agreed replacement slot. Please confirm someone is at the gate.” Bao answered that the gate was open. The pickup happened at 1:16. The customer did not complain about the covers themselves, and there is no evidence that they asked for a discount or a new delivery date before the original slot. The invoice has no late-pickup charge, either; the shop waived a possible internal handling charge because the missed handoff was ours.\n\nThere is some tempting noise in the thread. A different customer, Cinderline Fabrication, moved a collection from Wednesday to Friday that same week. Their note is pasted below the Saltmarsh messages because the dispatch mailbox groups everything under “collections.” That other change has nothing to do with Saltmarsh Rentals. Likewise, the administrator’s line about a changed sheet is true—the receiving entrance was changed—but it does not establish a changed collection date.\n\nForward from the job board export: “Disposition: customer postponement. Reason: updated receiving details.” This export copied the uncorrected job-card note. It did not independently verify the messages. The freight coordinator’s reply says, “Looks like customer-requested Friday move,” but Bao later wrote, “I should not have marked that; our gate caused the miss.” The coordinator’s impression and the copied disposition both need checking against the messages, not treating as fresh evidence.\n\nAiden’s cover note continues: “I need a clean answer for the weekly review. We are not trying to blame anyone; we just need the record to show whether the original arrangement changed at the customer’s request. The equipment check, key handoff, and rack move were all shop-side issues. There was no flood, road closure, or carrier breakdown. The driver reached the location on time. I have left the customer’s original Thursday message in the chain so nobody has to rely on my memory.”\n\nAt the bottom is Bao’s final correction to the production list: “Please replace the earlier note with ‘shop unavailable for Thursday collection; customer accepted Friday replacement slot.’ I am sorry the first summary made it sound like Saltmarsh asked us to move it.”",
